What Is Mobile App Penetration Testing?
Mobile app penetration testing is a cybersecurity assessment designed to identify vulnerabilities in Android and iOS applications. Security professionals perform authorized and controlled testing to evaluate application security, authentication, data storage, communication, APIs, and other components.
The objective is to discover potential weaknesses before attackers can exploit them and provide organizations with practical recommendations for improving application security.
Why Businesses Need Mobile App Penetration Testing
Mobile applications can handle sensitive information such as customer details, login credentials, payment information, and business data. Security weaknesses could allow attackers to access or manipulate this information.
Professional mobile app penetration testing can help Sri Lankan organizations:
- Identify vulnerabilities in Android and iOS applications.
- Test authentication and authorization mechanisms.
- Detect insecure data storage and information exposure.
- Evaluate API and backend security.
- Identify weaknesses in application configurations.
- Assess secure communication between applications and servers.
- Reduce the risk of unauthorized access and data breaches.
- Improve overall mobile application security.
